WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.490
- First of all, thank you so much for

00:00:01.490 --> 00:00:02.440
what you're doing for us.

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:04.180
We, I mean, I've always appreciated it

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:06.652
but obviously we all
appreciate it way more now.

00:00:06.652 --> 00:00:09.569
(inspiring music)

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.000
- We talk about nurses,
other people that are

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.702
that make our entire country
work, our entire society work.

00:00:16.702 --> 00:00:17.535
- Yeah.

00:00:17.535 --> 00:00:19.190
- And we ought to be so grateful to them

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:22.530
for persisting and persevering
through all these challenges

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:24.630
and doing their best for our young people.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.640
- I'm a neonatal intensive care nurse,

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:34.500
And so I've seen firsthand
moms being separated

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.530
from their babies.

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:39.580
And so

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:42.373
that was tough, and is still tough for me.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.540
- So I'm a nurse at
Fox Chase Cancer Center

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:49.760
And this started when a patient came in

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:53.610
with a young patient with
metastatic disease and he was

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:57.560
in so much pain and it was
his birthday and he was alone.

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:00.100
Couldn't have family here with him

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:02.890
and I just felt the need
to give him something

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:04.683
and celebrate his birthday.

00:01:07.592 --> 00:01:09.670
- And so my mom actually
grabbed a trash bag

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:11.570
and was just triaging patients basically

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:14.240
and writing down what
medications do you need?

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:19.100
Because imagine someone who
is elder and needs oxygen.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:20.880
How could they run out of that fire,

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.490
grabbing their oxygen
tank or their medications.

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:26.160
- We value your dedication,
your service, everything.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:27.520
So on behalf of our show

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:29.200
I wanna present to you with this check.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:30.610
The show is donating 5,000.

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:31.610
I'm gonna donate 15.

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:34.350
And we love what you're doing

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:36.060
and we wanna see you keep doing it.

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:38.270
So that's why we're just
gonna give you $2,500

00:01:38.270 --> 00:01:39.320
just to help out.

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:41.080
- Oh my God that's awesome.

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:44.110
- We're gonna send all
of you on a five day trip

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:47.320
to Westgate Town Center Resort in Orlando.

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:48.990
Would you be into this kind of vacation?

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:50.819
- Oh yeah.

00:01:50.819 --> 00:01:52.363
(laughing)

00:01:52.363 --> 00:01:55.196
(inspiring music)

